cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EPSILON in research, teaching, or a reproducibility exercise, please cite this software."
title: "EPSILON: A Quantitative Evidence Instrument"
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-13
authors:
  - family-names: "Goehner"
    given-names: "Dresden E."
abstract: >-
  EPSILON is an open-source quantitative evidence instrument for testing whether
  a market conclusion survives nearby changes in execution costs, timing,
  sampling windows, and universe assumptions. It keeps claims, rejection rules,
  provenance, perturbations, outcomes, and limitations attached to each result.
repository-code: "https://github.com/DresdenGman/EPSILON-trading-simulator"
url: "https://epsilonfield.space"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - quantitative research
  - sensitivity analysis
  - reproducible research
  - falsifiability
  - backtesting
  - decision science
